00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
stratford-on-avon district council is  currently consulting on the site  allocations plan  this short video explains policy snap 6  in the site allocations plan which  relates to self and custom-built housing  self-built housing is where people  directly organize the design and  construction of new homes for themselves  while custom-built housing is where  individuals or groups work with a  specific developer  to build new homes that meet their  specific aspirations  in 2015 the government introduced a  requirement for councils to give  planning permission for enough plots to  meet the demand for self and  custom-built house building in their  area  since 2016 councils have been required  to keep a register of those who are  seeking plots of land  in their area for this purpose  in june 2020 stratford or nathan  district council had 151 people on its  register  with an average of 36 individuals  applying each calendar year  the policy within the site allocations  plan sets out how the need within  stratford-on-avon district  up to 2031 can be achieved  all self and custom build plots will be  offered in the first  instance to people that have a local  connection through either living  working or by having close family within  the district  the council will encourage this type of  housing to be zero carbon  with a minimum carbon reduction of 31  that can be achieved through measures  such as low  carbon heating schemes renewable energy  and better fabric standards  applicants will need to submit a  sustainability statement with their  planning applications  outlining how their development will  meet this low carbon standard  to ensure high quality developments  applicants for self and custom build  sites will be expected to prepare design  codes or plot passports  these should cover such matters as  phasing building form  density footprints of dwellings building  lines  materials boundary treatment public open  space  landscaping and waste facilities  there are three ways in which new self  and custom-built housing will be  provided  as long as they meet certain criteria  firstly as an integral part of the new  settlements at gaydon lighthound heath  and long martin airfield  secondly on suitable unallocated sites  within or adjacent to the built-up area  boundaries of settlements  thirdly on 11 sites allocated  specifically for this purpose within the  plan  there are 11 sites in the plan that are  solely allocated  for self and custom built homes all of  which lie directly adjacent to the  relevant built up area boundaries and  relate well to the physical form of the  settlement  these sites have been promoted for this  type of housing by the landowner  and you can see the full list in the  description of this video as well as in  the sap  i hope this has provided you with an  overview to our approach to meeting the  district's need for self and custom  build housing  you can find out more in the site  allocations plan and submit any comments  you have  by visiting our website at  www.stratford.org  dot uk forward slash sappo
 

